{"base_rate":0.2924901185770751,"brier":0.17247338603425563,"bss":0.16655224470280316,"bss_hi":0.26442350858717417,"bss_lo":0.06838402707447806,"country":"CA","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.12725955204216072,"ess":570.1537357804688,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Winnipeg</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Winnipeg rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 7 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (94%), believe about\n<b>71%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>5%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 759 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nWINNIPEG 0.3 S, 1.4 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.17, ranked 97 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(73&ndash;103) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>202</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>11%</b></td><td class='num'>99</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>16%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>10%</td><td class='num'><b>21%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>18%</td><td class='num'><b>36%</b></td><td class='num'>81</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'><b>62%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>64%</td><td class='num'><b>55%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>94%</td><td class='num'><b>71%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">7 of 8 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Winnipeg</b> <span class=\"muted\">CA</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">7 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.17</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>73&ndash;103\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>759 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Winnipeg &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Winnipeg\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 63.18484848484849,367.2929292929293 72.5277922077922,348.9090909090909 91.70478873239438,320.4788732394366 122.50666666666666,283.1358024691358 178.40657894736842,219.1578947368421 283.58184210526315,113.78947368421052 389.6566233766233,22.727272727272748 389.6566233766233,60.54545454545456 283.58184210526315,190.42105263157896 178.40657894736842,295.7894736842105 122.50666666666666,346.04938271604937 91.70478873239438,371.7464788732394 72.5277922077922,382.0 63.18484848484849,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"275.5335968379447\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"275.5335968379447\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,362.1782178217822 63.18484848484849,341.55555555555554 72.5277922077922,325.27272727272725 91.70478873239438,305.09859154929575 122.50666666666666,251.679012345679 178.40657894736842,156.89473684210526 283.58184210526315,180.84210526315786 389.6566233766233,122.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 5% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 202 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"362.1782178217822\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 1%&amp;#10;It rained 11% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 99 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"63.18484848484849\" cy=\"341.55555555555554\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 16% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"72.5277922077922\" cy=\"325.27272727272725\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 10%&amp;#10;It rained 21% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"91.70478873239438\" cy=\"305.09859154929575\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 18%&amp;#10;It rained 36% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 81 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"122.50666666666666\" cy=\"251.679012345679\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 34%&amp;#10;It rained 62% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"178.40657894736842\" cy=\"156.89473684210526\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 64%&amp;#10;It rained 55% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"283.58184210526315\" cy=\"180.84210526315786\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 94%&amp;#10;It rained 71% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"389.6566233766233\" cy=\"122.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(29%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Winnipeg the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.31) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.02).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>183</td><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'>0.016</td><td class='num'>14.1%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>35%</td><td class='num'>0.052</td><td class='num'>21.2%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>179</td><td class='num'>22%</td><td class='num'>0.266</td><td class='num'>7.8%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>217</td><td class='num'>26%</td><td class='num'>0.312</td><td class='num'>5.1%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":49.8844,"lon":-97.14704,"n":759,"n_cities":109,"name":"Winnipeg","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.01,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":202,"obs":0.054455445544554455,"sig":true},{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.01,"mean":0.014646464646464645,"n":99,"obs":0.1111111111111111,"sig":true},{"hi":0.07,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.041038961038961035,"n":77,"obs":0.15584415584415584,"sig":true},{"hi":0.14,"lo":0.07,"mean":0.09521126760563381,"n":71,"obs":0.2112676056338028,"sig":true},{"hi":0.25,"lo":0.14,"mean":0.1822222222222222,"n":81,"obs":0.35802469135802467,"sig":true},{"hi":0.46,"lo":0.25,"mean":0.34013157894736845,"n":76,"obs":0.618421052631579,"sig":true},{"hi":0.8,"lo":0.46,"mean":0.6372368421052632,"n":76,"obs":0.5526315789473685,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.8,"mean":0.9368831168831167,"n":77,"obs":0.7142857142857143,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":1.4,"rank":97,"rank_hi":103.0,"rank_lo":73.0,"reliability":0.021396587975885534,"resolution":0.05780278771845752,"slug":"winnipeg","station":"WINNIPEG 0.3 S","timezone":"America/Winnipeg"}